    "other": "Published D total minus the four complete named employment groups. Negative and incomplete employment residuals remain unavailable. The identical four groups define the corresponding INDSTAT value-added residual. Negative value-added residuals remain signed."
  },
  "grouping": "Sum the exact ISIC Rev.3 divisions. For a combined code, include the numeric anchor once only if the publisher identifies all included divisions within the group, and no numeric secondary is counted separately. Check all reported combination notes for overlap across the group boundary even when a secondary lacks the corresponding flag. Incomplete, overlapping or cross-group combinations and division-specific coverage/confidentiality footnotes withhold the group. UNIDO estimates remain identified. For both employment and value added the same industry grouping is applied independently. A published division footnoted as partial is withheld. Duplicate numeric records merge their notes; records with conflicting values or industry coverage are withheld.",
  "employmentShares": "Use 100 times the tabulated industry count divided by a positive published D total. Withhold the share if the component exceeds the total. Raw counts may be fractional, particularly UNIDO estimates and FTEs. Preserve published precision in the source archive.",
  "interpretation": "A count difference describes net change in reported employment. Employment and output shares use their respective manufacturing totals; share change is measured in percentage points. Employment and value added use INDSTAT establishment data. Joint comparisons require matching scope and reference-period notes within the same economy and year. Explicitly distinct source bases, e.g. national accounts versus an employment survey, withhold the joint comparison. Unspecified notes do not prove equal coverage. A share change alone does not establish absolute output growth or individual job transitions.",
  "basis": "Year-specific employment concepts, scope and reference periods take priority over variable- and country-level notes. Reported concepts distinguish persons engaged and full-time equivalents from the baseline Employees variable. Full definitions and native notes remain available. Blank scope/definitions mean the publisher supplies no corresponding note.",
  "comparableChanges": "Require exact endpoints and a common country-specific contiguous comparison segment for employment changes. Segments split when effective employment definition, concept, scope or reference period changes, at flagged methodological breaks, and at source-reported alternating census coverage. Explicit changes between survey and national-account sources also split segments. Native source warnings can affect comparisons within a segment. Shares require independent valid denominators.",
  "output": "Use source variable 20 and native local-currency v, not the dollar conversion u. Divide each grouped current-price value-added amount by its positive D total for the same country and year. Retain signed amounts and shares outside 0–100. No nominal currency growth statistic is calculated here. WDI composition shares have a different publication and may differ from these direct INDSTAT calculations.",
  "outputComparability": "Use an independent value-added regime based on reported valuation, scope, reference period and applicable break notes. Joint changes require unchanged employment and output regimes and compatible source scopes and reference periods at both endpoints. Native source notes may describe further limitations.",
